docs/01-landscape.md:220:**R7. Default palettes fail contrast, color-vision checks, or both.** The colors of the six donut slices, in order, scored for contrast against white (WCAG 1.4.11 asks 3:1 for graphical objects that are needed to understand the content) and for the smallest pairwise difference in OKLab under normal vision and Machado-simulated deficiencies. Repeated colors count as a pair with zero difference.
docs/01-landscape.md:222:| Library | Colors of the six slices | Distinct | Below 3:1 on white | Closest pair: normal | Protanopia | Deuteranopia | Tritanopia |
docs/01-landscape.md:233:ApexCharts is the only one whose colors all reach 3:1, and its sixth slice has the same blue as its first, next to it on the ring. Recharts has no palette (every line is `#3182bd` and every sector `#808080` until the author assigns colors); the repeat above comes from cycling the four colors its examples use, which is **authored**. uPlot has no palette. Plotly's orange and green are nearly identical under simulated protanopia (0.007). ECharts was scored from its option palette, not from rendered pixels.
